---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: Astro uses this layout component below.
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About | plansplease"
  description="plansplease gives the useful pages made by coding agents a place to land."
  activePath="about"
>
  <section class="about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="about-hero-content">
      <span class="about-badge">Our Mission</span>
      <h1 id="about-title">A place for the useful things agents make.</h1>
      <p class="about-lead">
        plansplease exists because AI agents are writing brilliant, full-featured web applications,
        but chat interfaces were never designed to preserve software.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-content">
    <div class="about-narrative">
      <h2>The Gap Between Prompt and Permanence</h2>
      <p>
        Every day, engineers and makers ask LLMs to build interactive tools: financial sensitivity
        calculators, prototype UI components, research briefs with interactive charts, and internal
        utilities. The model outputs a complete HTML file in seconds.
      </p>
      <p>
        And then what happens? You scroll down, the chat compacts, or you close the tab. The tool is
        lost. If you do save it, it sits in your <code>Downloads</code> folder, broken when clicked
        because of browser security sandboxes, or requiring an hour of boilerplate repo setup just
        to view.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="values-grid">
      <article class="value-card">
        <h3>It starts on your machine</h3>
        <p>
          The CLI gives any standalone HTML file or page folder an instant local URL via a lightweight
          loopback daemon. Iterate with your agent in real-time without polluting your project setup.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="value-card">
        <h3>The cloud keeps the useful copy</h3>
        <p>
          Our managed workspace provides a permanent, authenticated home for your agent artifacts.
          Access your interactive dashboards and tools from any machine, anytime.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="value-card">
        <h3>Lightweight by design</h3>
        <p>
          A single-purpose page does not need a full Next.js application, Docker container, or CI/CD
          pipeline to be useful. Start with the standalone artifact in front of you.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="value-card">
        <h3>Built in the open</h3>
        <p>
          The core runtime and CLI are 100% open source on
          <a href="https://github.com/abijith-suresh/planview">GitHub</a>. We build with the
          developer community to establish the standard runtime for agent web artifacts.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    padding: clamp(4rem, 7vh, 6rem) 0 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--night-border);
  }

  .about-hero-content {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .about-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: var(--iris-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--iris-border);
    color: var(--iris);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .about-hero h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4.4vw, 3.6rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .about-lead {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .about-content {
    padding: 4.5rem 0;
  }

  .about-narrative {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .about-narrative h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .about-narrative p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .about-narrative code {
    color: var(--mint);
    background: var(--night-card);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .values-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .value-card {
    padding: 2.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--night-card);
  }

  .value-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .value-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .value-card a {
    color: var(--mint);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .values-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
